==Icelandic==
===Etymology===
From ''[[gamall]]'' (meaning "[[old]]") + ''[[dags]]'', the {{gen}} {{singular}} of ''[[dagur]]'' meaning "[[day]]". Literally meaning "of an [[old]] [[day]]".

===Adjective===
'''gamaldags'''
# [[old-fashioned]]
#: ''Hann er svo '''gamaldags'''.''
#:: He is so '''old-fashioned'''.
# [[antiquated]], [[archaic]]
#: '''''Gamaldags''' stólar.''
#:: '''Antiquated''' chairs.
#: ''Hann notar mörg '''gamaldags''' orð.''
#:: He uses many '''archaic''' words.

